    Terraform — aws_network_acl:

      resource "aws_network_acl" "app" {
        vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id

        ingress {
          rule_no    = 100
          protocol   = "tcp"
          action     = "allow"
          cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
          from_port  = 443
          to_port    = 443
        }
      }

    Out of band — aws_network_acl:

      aws ec2 replace-network-acl-entry --network-acl-id <acl-id> --rule-number <n> --protocol tcp --rule-action allow --ingress --cidr-block 10.0.0.0/16 --port-range From=443,To=443

    Note (aws_network_acl): Same shape as the port 21 fix, and the same two
    traps: a deny rule at a lower number does not clear this finding because the
    control reads allow entries, and network ACLs are stateless so the ephemeral
    egress range must survive the edit. Closing 20 without closing 21 leaves FTP
